  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Xifaxan (rifaximin) criteria effective 2016-10-03. Strengths: 200 mg and 550 mg tablets. Clinical evidence requires manual review.",
    "IBS-D course count means previously completed 14-day courses in the rolling 365 days. The explicit denial after three completed courses controls the approval wording “has not exceeded three”; a fourth course is denied. Inpatient initiation substitutes only for Rome III criteria, not adult age, diagnosis or course limit.",
    "Initial authorization (notes only): TD 3 days; HE 1 year; IBS-D 14 days.",
    "Reauthorization (notes only): TD and HE require all initial criteria and documented positive clinical response. TD allows three reauthorizations (4 courses total per rolling 365 days) with additional travel. HE may be approved for 1 year. IBS-D requires positive clinical response with improvement in Rome III symptoms, symptom recurrence and other causes ruled out; may start 10 weeks after the end of the last course, up to 3 courses of 14 days per rolling 365 days. Renewal requires manual review.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 200 mg TD 3 tablets/day for up to 3 days; 550 mg HE 2 tablets/day; 550 mg IBS-D 3 tablets/day for up to 14 days. Quantity and duration require manual review; max_units is null. PDL status unknown; no linked alternatives."
  ],
